    "b-rulebook-intro-2": {
      "id": "b-rulebook-intro-2",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "R1-R10 govern every agent-produced board. They distill the eight reference boards in "
        },
        {
          "insert": "canvases/",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " (agent-flows-2, bubba-voice, claude-code-researcher, gc-decomp-harness, ink-diagrams, intent-classification-1 and -2, and v2-flow) and are enforced through the single "
        },
        {
          "insert": "Calm and uniform — uniformity is information",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true,
            "reference": {
              "kind": "source",
              "path": "packages/canvas-agent/src/catalog/layout-editor/context/style-guide/aesthetic.ts",
              "symbol": "style"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " aesthetic topic and the constraints inside the four workflow phases. The system prompt has six top-level sections (purpose, state_structure, core_philosophy, workflow, success_criteria, and quality_checklist), and phase constraints carry the operational rules. Reference-board evidence is cited inline where a rule leans on it, and the runtime surfaces named below own behavior."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-rulebook-naming-3": {
      "id": "b-rulebook-naming-3",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "The capability blocks define the four entity kinds and their operations. The op path applies the mechanical invariants: geometry patches are complete finite rectangles, every number a gesture writes to geometry lands on the agent's 20 grid, section membership is reconciled from geometry, sections keep the geometry they are given until fit_section closes one, and the locked page frame is protected. The "
        },
        {
          "insert": "covered-content",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true,
            "reference": {
              "kind": "source",
              "path": "packages/canvas-agent/src/board/lints/rules/covered-content.ts"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ", "
        },
        {
          "insert": "containment",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true,
            "reference": {
              "kind": "source",
              "path": "packages/canvas-agent/src/board/lints/rules/containment.ts"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ", "
        },
        {
          "insert": "broken-edges",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true,
            "reference": {
              "kind": "source",
              "path": "packages/canvas-agent/src/board/lints/rules/broken-edges.ts"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ", "
        },
        {
          "insert": "crowding",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true,
            "reference": {
              "kind": "source",
              "path": "packages/canvas-agent/src/board/lints/rules/crowding.ts"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ", "
        },
        {
          "insert": "unreadable-labels",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true,
            "reference": {
              "kind": "source",
              "path": "packages/canvas-agent/src/board/lints/rules/unreadable-labels.ts"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ", and "
        },
        {
          "insert": "clipped-text",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true,
            "reference": {
              "kind": "source",
              "path": "packages/canvas-agent/src/board/lints/rules/clipped-text.ts"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " lints judge production geometry. The "
        },
        {
          "insert": "label-is-prose",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true,
            "reference": {
              "kind": "source",
              "path": "packages/canvas-agent/src/board/lints/rules/label-is-prose.ts"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " and "
        },
        {
          "insert": "detail-too-long",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true,
            "reference": {
              "kind": "source",
              "path": "packages/canvas-agent/src/board/lints/rules/detail-too-long.ts"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " lints judge object text against the name and detail convention: a short name plus at most one detail line, with prose on a sticky. Every finding in the edited scope, error or warning, blocks a committed finalize. A fixable finding includes ready-to-send "
        },
        {
          "insert": "suggested op:",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " JSON."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-rulebook-rules-heading-4": {
      "id": "b-rulebook-rules-heading-4",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "The ten rules"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-rulebook-idx-r1-5": {
      "id": "b-rulebook-idx-r1-5",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {
        "ordered": false
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "R1 — The 20 grid",
          "attributes": {
            "reference": {
              "kind": "doc",
              "path": "10-system-design/60-layout-rulebook/01-r1-the-20-grid",
              "label": "R1 — The 20 grid"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ": object geometry is quantized to the agent's 20 grid. The grid is a snap unit, not a spacing prescription."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-rulebook-idx-r2-6": {
      "id": "b-rulebook-idx-r2-6",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {
        "ordered": false
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "R2 — The spacing ladder",
          "attributes": {
            "reference": {
              "kind": "doc",
              "path": "10-system-design/60-layout-rulebook/02-r2-the-spacing-ladder",
              "label": "R2 — The spacing ladder"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ": each peer group repeats one exact gap. The ladder names every rung from 48px section padding up to the 160px section gutter, and the crowding warning supplies the corridor floor rather than a target gap."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-rulebook-idx-r3-7": {
      "id": "b-rulebook-idx-r3-7",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {
        "ordered": false
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "R3 — Section trim",
          "attributes": {
            "reference": {
              "kind": "doc",
              "path": "10-system-design/60-layout-rulebook/03-r3-section-trim",
              "label": "R3 — Section trim"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ": sections supply grouping and addressability, and children keep air from borders. A frame is closed around its contents with fit_section when the region is done."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-rulebook-idx-r4-8": {
      "id": "b-rulebook-idx-r4-8",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {
        "ordered": false
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "R4 — grid: repeated-cell tables",
          "attributes": {
            "reference": {
              "kind": "doc",
              "path": "10-system-design/60-layout-rulebook/04-r4-grid",
              "label": "R4 — grid: repeated-cell tables"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ": repeated peers share the largest required size, one exact gap, and centers on a line, copied from digest geometry."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-rulebook-idx-r5-9": {
      "id": "b-rulebook-idx-r5-9",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {
        "ordered": false
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "R5 — align: cross-branch registers",
          "attributes": {
            "reference": {
              "kind": "doc",
              "path": "10-system-design/60-layout-rulebook/05-r5-align",
              "label": "R5 — align: cross-branch registers"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ": peer alignment is a deliberate visual signal, copied exactly and judged from each pushed render."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-rulebook-idx-r6-10": {
      "id": "b-rulebook-idx-r6-10",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {
        "ordered": false
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "R6 — fan: hub over children",
          "attributes": {
            "reference": {
              "kind": "doc",
              "path": "10-system-design/60-layout-rulebook/06-r6-fan",
              "label": "R6 — fan: hub over children"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ": a parent centers over peer children while their repeated gap leaves a readable wire corridor."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-rulebook-idx-r7-11": {
      "id": "b-rulebook-idx-r7-11",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {
        "ordered": false
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "R7 — hug: margin rails that never stretch",
          "attributes": {
            "reference": {
              "kind": "doc",
              "path": "10-system-design/60-layout-rulebook/07-r7-hug",
              "label": "R7 — hug: margin rails that never stretch"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ": content-sized side regions keep air around their contents and live in sections rather than stretching across unused space."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-rulebook-idx-r8-12": {
      "id": "b-rulebook-idx-r8-12",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {
        "ordered": false
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "R8 — Size semantics",
          "attributes": {
            "reference": {
              "kind": "doc",
              "path": "10-system-design/60-layout-rulebook/08-r8-size-semantics",
              "label": "R8 — Size semantics"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ": a box's content is a short name plus at most one detail line, and content determines size from one shared 288×96 target. Peers match the largest member, and deliberate size differences communicate importance or exception."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-rulebook-idx-r9-13": {
      "id": "b-rulebook-idx-r9-13",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {
        "ordered": false
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "R9 — Feedback edges and detours",
          "attributes": {
            "reference": {
              "kind": "doc",
              "path": "10-system-design/60-layout-rulebook/09-r9-feedback-edges",
              "label": "R9 — Feedback edges and detours"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ": returns use flow-facing anchors, direct labels, and minimally steered routes through clear corridors."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-rulebook-idx-r10-14": {
      "id": "b-rulebook-idx-r10-14",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {
        "ordered": false
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "R10 — What the language refuses to say",
          "attributes": {
            "reference": {
              "kind": "doc",
              "path": "10-system-design/60-layout-rulebook/10-r10-what-the-language-refuses-to-say",
              "label": "R10 — What the language refuses to say"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ": abstract align, fan, and lattice relations are not operation fields. Complete geometry carries the placement, and fresh digests plus renders carry the evidence."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-rulebook-lab-heading-19": {
      "id": "b-rulebook-lab-heading-19",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
